Force the server's remote UI self-update off.

Upstream leaves the remote UI update check on by default and the
Tauri shell never passes --ui-no-update, so a running server would
fetch UI assets over the network and overwrite the RPM payload.
RPM owns updates: pass the flag alongside the other serve
arguments (the desktop updater itself is already inert without a
signing key).

--- a/packages/tauri-app/src-tauri/src/cli_manager.rs	2026-10-30 18:28:01.392985244 +0100
+++ b/packages/tauri-app/src-tauri/src/cli_manager.rs	2026-10-30 18:28:01.404986591 +0100
@@ -1735,6 +1735,9 @@
             auth_cookie_name.to_string(),
             "--generate-token".to_string(),
             "--unrestricted-root".to_string(),
+            // Distro build: the server's remote UI self-update stays on by
+            // default upstream; RPM owns updates, so force it off here.
+            "--ui-no-update".to_string(),
         ];
 
         if dev {
